<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
         The shape every adaptive icon is clipped to.

         AdaptiveIconDrawable parses this into the clip path it applies to all
         of them, so changing it here changes every icon on the device at once
         - system, preinstalled and user-installed alike - without touching a
         single one of them individually.

         This is a regular octagon: corner cut 100/(2+sqrt 2) = 29.289, which
         makes all eight sides exactly 41.421 long. It is the octagonOS mark,
         at the scale of an app icon.

         Stock is a 100x100 rounded square with an 8-unit corner radius.

         The path is on the 100x100 viewport AdaptiveIconDrawable expects, and
         is closed. An octagon is also strictly larger than the circle Android
         documents as the safe zone, so no icon that was drawn correctly for
         the stock mask loses anything to this one.
    -->
    <string name="config_icon_mask" translatable="false">"M29.289,0 L70.711,0 L100,29.289 L100,70.711 L70.711,100 L29.289,100 L0,70.711 L0,29.289 Z"</string>
</resources>
